  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Differentiation II: displacement and distance travelled</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.1: Find when a particle is at rest, its displacement at a given time, and the total distance travelled when it changes direction twice.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question A5 in Section A of Chapter 1 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Mechanics 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: the distance-against-displacement idea is set with a cubic displacement and differentiation, with new numbers and diagnostics.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
